(505271, 48835, 6624, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>This image is perilously close to being a photograph of someone else''s work but the fact that the flag is juxtaposed saves it.  It is an interesting juxtaposition raising questions about war, patriotism, faith.  I think that the title is a bit unwieldy but that is a matter of taste.  I find myself wanting to turn the image - to push the right hand side back in order to change the angle of view. That is reflective of the difficulty in putting the elements of this together and wanting a clearer statement from the image. Perhaps see more of the flag and less of the massive flagpole. The color and clarity are good.  It''s a complex image and one that you may want to revisit.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club: This image is perilously close to being a photograph of someone else''s work but the fact that the flag is juxtaposed saves it.  It is an interesting juxtaposition raising questions about war, patriotism, faith.  I think that the title is a bit unwieldy but that is a matter of taste.  I find myself wanting to turn the image - to push the right hand side back in order to change the angle of view. That is reflective of the difficulty in putting the elements of this together and wanting a clearer statement from the image. Perhaps see more of the flag and less of the massive flagpole. The color and clarity are good.  It''s a complex image and one that you may want to revisit.', '2003-12-06 10:29:16.000000', NULL, 0),
