(505522, 48835, 4793, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful, well done shot.</td>', 'This is a beautiful, well done shot.', '2003-12-06 16:35:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(505623, 48883, 6999, '<td valign="top">despite being pipped for the only moderately disappointing 4th place, I was still glad to see this shot placed here: I aways look for your photos JJ, and was beginning to think you''d packed it in after not entering the last two or three challenges. <br/> <br/>This two-thirds foreground is becoming distinctive of your work: this one works particularly well I think - perhaps because the lower two thirds divides itself into a near-ground and mid-ground area, so that there''s three levels of detail going on. There''s something of the combination of brass and steel - which is an enormously photogenic matching of metals - in the colours you''ve worked with too: just a muted version of the blue/orange complementries really.<br/> <br/>Perhaps a grouping of your photo and mine, with the garnish of a few good friends, would be the thing to most give thanks for.<br/> <br/>Ed<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-12-29 09:44:20.</i></td>', 'despite being pipped for the only moderately disappointing 4th place, I was still glad to see this shot placed here: I aways look for your photos JJ, and was beginning to think you''d packed it in after not entering the last two or three challenges.  This two-thirds foreground is becoming distinctive of your work: this one works particularly well I think - perhaps because the lower two thirds divides itself into a near-ground and mid-ground area, so that there''s three levels of detail going on. There''s something of the combination of brass and steel - which is an enormously photogenic matching of metals - in the colours you''ve worked with too: just a muted version of the blue/orange complementries really. Perhaps a grouping of your photo and mine, with the garnish of a few good friends, would be the thing to most give thanks for. Ed', '2003-12-06 19:29:11.000000', '2003-12-29 09:44:20.000000', 0),
(505645, 48839, 2170, '<td valign="top">congrats, dude!</td>', 'congrats, dude!', '2003-12-06 20:52:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(505699, 48824, 6477, '<td valign="top">I like this "laughing Buddha" shot. Sorry not so many people could get what you mean here. And thank you for share the Buddha teachings in your comments.</td>', 'I like this "laughing Buddha" shot. Sorry not so many people could get what you mean here. And thank you for share the Buddha teachings in your comments.', '2003-12-06 23:12:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(505761, 48840, 14001, '<td valign="top">This shot I''m pretty amazed at how low it scored.  Not that I can''t see why, but just suprised.  Technically the setup has it''s issues, that''s for sure, and certainly can be downgraded because of that, so I''m not complaining.<br/> <br/>It''s just that catching a baby smilling in his sleep on film is pretty unusual, and considering I shot it hand-held with an on-camera flash I was happy with how it turned-out.  Then the blurr added to the feel of him sleeping.<br/> <br/>Spontaneity doesn''t seem to get much credit ''round here.  OK.  Live and learn.</td>', 'This shot I''m pretty amazed at how low it scored.  Not that I can''t see why, but just suprised.  Technically the setup has it''s issues, that''s for sure, and certainly can be downgraded because of that, so I''m not complaining. It''s just that catching a baby smilling in his sleep on film is pretty unusual, and considering I shot it hand-held with an on-camera flash I was happy with how it turned-out.  Then the blurr added to the feel of him sleeping. Spontaneity doesn''t seem to get much credit ''round here.  OK.  Live and learn.', '2003-12-07 02:50:41.000000', NULL, 0),
